- **The closure, stated as a property (assert it):** *every notes value `SaveTriage` can store passes `WellFormed()`.* The API trims with `string.Trim()` and refuses `HasControl`; so `WellFormed` must use the same `Trim()` (not `TrimStart`/`TrimEnd` or a char list) and the same control rule, and must accept notes with interior LF, CR and TAB. A row-8 style assertion plus the existing restart row (`Writes_to_different_fields_...`) are the proof; if your WellFormed refuses a sidecar the API wrote, the store would drop its own state at start-up: that is the failure to avoid.
- **Suggested shape (yours to improve inside the property):** `Notes is { } n && n.Length <= FeedbackEndpoints.MaxNotes && n == n.Trim() && !FeedbackEndpoints.HasControl(n)` with `HasControl` made `internal static`. State in STATUS under DESIGN which you chose and why.
